[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186176049,
      "id": "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9",
      "title": "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4ff75327-0256-57ae-9769-b9a4627cb236",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain is all real numbers.\n- **II.** The function is positive throughout $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi,n\\pi).$\n- **III.** The least positive period is $\\pi.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "22e6fd7f-20b1-50e5-9486-d68c08d5721f",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "38180c8f-f162-50c7-8ec1-9f8f4a9b994b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "f81071ba-7edc-5e8f-93c4-4c1defade159",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "38180c8f-f162-50c7-8ec1-9f8f4a9b994b"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "2f7b477d-3777-5537-bb4d-b9c3d3b927d8",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "f2e9ed08-4d33-5f4a-bd0d-6b54c593105e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "b88094e3-8880-59cf-bacf-42220764cda0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "f2e9ed08-4d33-5f4a-bd0d-6b54c593105e"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e17f0199-5c86-5554-b35c-db81a70f5482",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "fde579dd-0833-5762-b752-2305551aba06",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "a49661b7-2064-5f27-9c18-472bf6dc529d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "a49661b7-2064-5f27-9c18-472bf6dc529d"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176049/tangent.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is defined everywhere except where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is positive on $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$ and negative on $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},0).$ The period is $\\pi,$ so these signs repeat after each integer multiple of $\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph repeats after a horizontal shift of $\\pi,$ and no smaller positive shift repeats the whole graph. Therefore, the least positive period is $\\pi.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."
    },
